<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kawila</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1742–1816</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kawila was a prince of Lampang who in the 1770s allied with the Thonburi Kingdom of Siam and helped drive the Burmese out of Lan Na. He rebuilt the depopulated city of Chiang Mai from 1796, bringing in war captives as settlers, and ruled it as a Siamese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a>. His descendants governed Chiang Mai, Lampang and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lamphun">Lamphun</a> until the twentieth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kawila.jpg" alt="Kawila" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown, Current owner is Chiang Mai Art and Culture Centre (หอศิลปวัฒนธรรมเชียงใหม่) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Kawila.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
